values ('e5a6b7c8-9d0e-4f75-8a45-5b6c7d8e9f05', 'history-and-systems-of-psychology', 'History and Systems of Psychology', 'Frame psychology''s history as an active interpretation of ideas, institutions, evidence, power, and professional identity. Topics trace questions about mind, knowledge, body, soul, behavior, and experience before laboratory science; how measurement, sensory science, physiology, and evolution helped make psychology scientific; structuralism, functionalism, Gestalt psychology, psychoanalysis, and behaviorism; measurement, testing, and applied psychology; humanistic and existential thought; the cognitive revolution; biological, neuroscience, evolutionary, and embodied perspectives; professional psychology; who was included, excluded, studied, pathologized, and erased; and psychology as a pluralistic science navigating integration, ethics, reproducibility, culture, technology, and public impact.');

