ries and methods."}, {"id": "de414e04-9ec8-4521-881c-996cbb4e2657", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Replication and open science", "children": [{"id": "11079e83-521f-438e-b44f-cadf2320216c", "type": "concept", "title": "Replication crisis"}, {"id": "c51a31d7-b74c-47a6-a10a-adf1f1700e64", "type": "concept", "title": "Preregistration"}, {"id": "06c5cec4-eb3d-4647-929f-8f46c64e123f", "type": "concept", "title": "Open data"}, {"id": "108ae67b-65dc-41c4-9144-e3dbb4ebede7", "type": "concept", "title": "Registered reports"}], "description": "Recent reforms show how history continues through debates about evidence, transparency, and trust."}, {"id": "a0bff4f8-9fc5-4e38-9f9d-8ff25fd5ee21", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Future directions", "children": [{"id": "11b18fb4-cefa-4296-8fe6-cb3df97c975a", "type": "concept", "title": "AI and psychology"}, {"id": "da6886c8-3255-4b77-8c24-3a022f4f7b30", "type": "concept", "title": "Digital mental health"}, {"id": "c671675b-f462-43ba-a9ad-42a516222eb7", "type": "concept", "title": "Interdisciplinary science"}, {"id": "d68ad14b-9ee0-4a53-8e10-72737a191dbe", "type": "concept", "title": "Public psychology"}], "description": "Students end by connecting historical systems to emerging questions about technology, equity, interdisciplinarity, and public impact."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$hsysjson$::jsonb,
